A note on the hardware this firmware controls: this project involves a siren,
mains-adjacent 5V/12V wiring, and a home security system. The MIT license
above covers the software only. Building and operating the physical device is
entirely at your own risk — verify your own wiring, use appropriately rated
components and power supplies, and do not rely on this project as a
substitute for a certified security or medical-alert system where that
matters. See the "Known limitations & honest caveats" section of the README
for further detail.
